# 900-NRL-0021: Measured prepared incremental generation — done

**Type:** implementation, `NRL` · **Owner:** Codex (`codex/NRL-lab`) · **Priority:** P1 · **Status:** done (2026-10-26) · **Blocked by:** — · **Roadmap:** G; 900 T12 · **Constitution:** MC-5.2, MC-11.1, MC-11.11, MC-12.1, MC-12.2, MC-12.3, MC-12.4

## Problem

The maintainer requested the five autonomous extensions after the first T11 preparation and host T12/T13 results. Existing host evidence does not establish this extension or native execution.

## Plan

Reuse checked FFN views and scratch across prefill and greedy decoding, preserve reference execution and public transactional step semantics, and profile paired generation runs.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Identical full step logits and generated token IDs, including compressed paths; unchanged failure behavior; bounded paired measurements and explicit promotion decision.
- [x] Document the supported profile and limitations, run affected checks on the track branch, preserve reports, and submit an updated landing request.

## Related

- [900](../issues/900-neural-representation-lab.md), T12.
- [NRL](../nrl/README.md). Native T11 remains a separate APP dependency.

## Resolution

Added request-scoped prepared FFNs/scratch and a private append-only KV session with rollback on input, context and late numerical failure; retained the original reference and public external-state transaction. Promoted greedy generation only after the frozen paired study accepted identical IDs and a nonoverlapping host timing gain. Preserved pre-promotion, intermediate overlapping and final accepted reports; final median elapsed time 14.248 ms reference versus 9.985 ms prepared is host/workload-specific.

The final NRL profile passes on `b44fbc0d`: 95 host tests, four portable builds and all CLI cycles, including `--expanded`; new external oracles reproduce. [Evidence](../nrl/reports/five-extensions-2026-10-26.json). The full repository gate and code landing belong to the integrator; native T11 remains open.
